enterADeviceSyncPort165535_8ca6b1="Enter a device sync port (1–65535) and choose a listening scope. The app can start even if this setting is not saved; configure it later in App Settings and restart. Choose LAN for local IP access at http://NAS-LAN-IP:PORT. For remote access, forward a public IP or DDNS port to this NAS port, or use localhost with FRP, a reverse proxy or VPN forwarding to 127.0.0.1:PORT. HTTP is unencrypted by default; public exposure risks scanning and unauthorized access. Use HTTPS, a VPN or source restrictions and protect pairing codes. Restart this app from App Center after saving."
enterADeviceSyncPort165535_dbf8f6="Enter a device sync port (1–65535) and choose a listening scope. Choose LAN to use http://NAS-LAN-IP:PORT locally, with router port forwarding or DDNS for remote access. Alternatively choose localhost and forward to 127.0.0.1:PORT using FRP, a reverse proxy or VPN. HTTP is unencrypted by default; public exposure risks scanning and unauthorized access. Prefer HTTPS, a VPN or source restrictions and protect pairing codes. Do not expose unnecessary ports. Restart this app from App Center after saving."
